SUMMARY:Audubon bird walk at Fort Pickens
DESCRIPTION:The Francis M. Weston Audubon Society leads a guided bird walk
  at Battery Langdon in Fort Pickens. Winter birds are arriving\, so expec
 t scaup\, bufflehead and red-breasted merganser on the water and sparrows
  plus yellow-rumped warblers in the oaks. The walk is mostly even ground 
 with some loose sand. Registration is required and the walk is free\, but
  entering the national seashore costs a park fee.\nPrice: Free\nArea: Pen
 sacola Beach & Perdido\nTimes: Saturday 11/14 · 6:30 AM to 10:00 AM\nChe
 cked against the venue's own page on 2026-11-11\nhttps://coastaleventures
 .com/events/ev-fmwas-fort-pickens-bird-trip-1114.html
